  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "RuntimeSupervisor Result Envelope v1",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Date**: 2026-05-16",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Summary",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`RuntimeSupervisorResultEnvelope` is the canonical terminal evidence shape for supervised subprocess execution. It is built at the invocation boundary by `SupervisorCommandInvoker` from:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- terminal stream event classification - command and cwd digests - timing facts - output digests and byte counts - safe trace context - state machine projection facts",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The envelope is content-light and privacy-preserving. It does not carry raw stdout, raw stderr, raw argv strings, or raw cwd values.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Root Cause",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Before this slice, `RuntimeSupervisor` produced terminal stream events and `SupervisorCommandInvoker` converted those events into a flat result model. Downstream layers could only infer subprocess meaning by reinterpreting raw fields, which encouraged divergent vocabularies and duplicated result shapes.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Cleanup / Normalization",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This slice introduced a stable envelope model with a single terminal classification vocabulary:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `completed` - `failed` - `timed_out` - `killed` - `cancelled` - `spawn_failed` - `cleanup_failed` - `errored` - `refused`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The envelope also carries:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- command digest - cwd digest - output digest - timing - resource usage - safe error details - cleanup status - trace/evidence identifiers - state machine projection",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-14",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Semantics",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Existing caller-facing subprocess output behavior remains unchanged. The flat result still exposes stdout/stderr text to direct callers that expect it. The envelope is additive evidence, not a replacement for the user-facing result.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Tests",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Covered by:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `tests/runtime/test_runtime_supervisor_result_envelope.py` - `tests/runtime/test_runtime_supervisor.py` - `tests/runtime/test_runtime_supervisor_state_machine.py` - `tests/runtime/test_runtime_supervisor_teardown.py` - `tests/tracing/test_runtime_supervisor_tracing.py`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "These tests prove:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- success, non-zero exit, timeout, spawn failure, and cancellation all produce envelopes - privacy-sensitive fields are excluded from the envelope - trace classification stays aligned with the envelope classification - the state projection matches the terminal lifecycle - the envelope builder is pure",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-21",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Remaining Gaps",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The envelope is wired at the supervisor invocation boundary, and ToolRuntime now preserves it through subprocess-backed tool calls. Remaining downstream consumers still need to adopt it directly:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `validate` - desktop diagnostics - future `SubagentRuntime`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Those consumers currently still rely on the existing flat result contract.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
